; lisp: float-round-trip.lisp
; Every float prints, and its printed text reads back as the same float, bit
; for bit (sys/io/print.lisp, PRINT-FLONUM and FLONUM-DIGITS;
; sys/io/read.lisp, XR-FLOAT-BITS; lisp/float-round-trip.lisp).  SI:FRT-RUN
; round trips a sample and gives the number of floats that did not come
; back, the number tried, and up to three of them: the text, the float's
; exact value as (M E), M * 2^E, and what the text read back as or the
; error.  The samples are built from bits and exact integers: the extremes
; and the constants of both signs, the infinities, 2^-20, the singles nearest
; 6.02e23 and 1e-37, and the one above the least normal; 2^k of both signs
; for every k in range and the singles on each side of it; the singles
; nearest 10^k of both signs; 3000 pseudo-random normal singles of every
; exponent and sign from a seeded LCG; and 208 subnormals of both signs, 200
; of them pseudo-random.  The printer scaled a float outside
; [1e-3, 1e7) to [1, 10) by floating multiplication, losing bits, and
; printed the scaled float's digits: the most positive single printed as
; "3.4028237e38", which reads as infinity, and the least positive normal one
; as "1.1754943e-38", below it, which underflows; and it negated a positive
; float, which for a subnormal signalled "MINUS produced a result too small",
; as arithmetic makes no subnormal.  The reader underflows below the least
; normal single, as arithmetic does, so a subnormal prints as
; #.(SI:SINGLE-FLOAT-FROM-BITS #x...), as an infinity prints as its constant.
; Run with --compile --files sys/io/print.lisp,
; tools/system-check/lisp/float-round-trip.lisp on a band built before the
; change.
(si:frt-run :extremes) => (0 18)
(si:frt-run :powers-of-2) => (0 1522)
(si:frt-run :powers-of-10) => (0 152)
(si:frt-run :random 0 1500) => (0 1500)
(si:frt-run :random 1500 3000) => (0 1500)
(si:frt-run :subnormal) => (0 208)
(prin1-to-string (si:frt-from-bits 1)) => "#.(SI:SINGLE-FLOAT-FROM-BITS #x1)"
(prin1-to-string (si:frt-from-bits #x807FFFFF)) => "#.(SI:SINGLE-FLOAT-FROM-BITS #x807FFFFF)"
